  "solenoids": {
    "notes": [
      "System 11A D-11392 solenoid architecture: SOL1-8 controlled via U28 LS374 latch (1Q-8Q) gated through U20/U19 AND arrays.",
      "SOL9-16 controlled via direct PB bits through U18 (PB0-PB3 -> SOL9-12) and U17 (PB4-PB7 -> SOL13-16).",
      "Special solenoids SS1-SS6 (Sol17-22) have dedicated TIP122 drivers gated through U45/U50 logic.",
      "A/C RELAY (Sol12): Sol1-8 each have TWO coils -- an 'A' coil (pulsed when Sol12 de-energized) and a 'C' coil (pulsed when Sol12 energized). Sol12 relay selects which set is active. A-coils are standard playfield mechanics; C-coils are flashers.",
      "Solenoid test numbers (01-22) are the CPU's internal identifiers and take precedence over wiring table numbering where discrepancies exist. Known discrepancy: wiring table swaps Sol5/Sol6 vs. test numbers.",
      "Sol 8: test mode fires C-circuit (Left Dock Kickback). A-circuit is Right Single Drop Target Raise. Both coils share Sol 8 test number depending on Sol 12 relay state.",
      "Blown F4 fuse on Aux Driver board is a known failure mode for Special Solenoids 17-22.",
      "bcd_code: null throughout -- System 11A decode mechanism differs from Bally BCD. Actual PIA write values to be determined via scan_trace on live board.",
      "transistor field cross-references to D-11392 board JSON (System11A_Driver_Board_final.json) for driver path verification.",
      "Coil part numbers: AE-23-800 (23V 800-ohm hold), AE-24-900 (24V 900-ohm), AE-26-1200 (26V 1200-ohm)."
    ],
